ey behaviour:** Fails fast on lint errors — warnings do not block the build. Coverage report is available as a downloadable artifact on every run. Uses Node.js 24 with npm cache for speed.\n\n---\n\n### pr-check.yml — Pull Request Quality Gate\n\n**Triggers:** PR opened or updated targeting `develop` or `main`.\n\n**Jobs:**\n\n| Job | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| Quality Gate | Runs `npm run test:coverage`, enforces Jest coverage thresholds (90%), and posts a coverage summary comment directly on the PR. |\n\n**Key behaviour:** Blocks merge if coverage thresholds are not met. Coverage comment is updated on each new commit to the PR — no duplicate comments.\n\n---\n\n### cd-deploy.yml — Deploy to Development / SIT\n\n**Triggers:** - **Automatic:** Push to `develop` → deploys to Development (BKZK-002). - **Manual:** `workflow_dispatch` — choose target environment (`dev` or `sit`) and optionally force data or vendor data import.\n\n**Jobs and execution order:**\n\nnonedetect-changes\n├── lint-xml (runs if data/ or vendor/ changed)\n├── run-tests (always)\n├── deploy-code (always, needs run-tests)\n├── deploy-data (needs lint-xml + detect-changes, runs if data/core changed)\n│ └── Rebuild search index (RebuildALLSearchIndex — all sites)\n└── deploy-vendor-data (needs deploy-data, runs if data/vendor changed)\n\n**Job details:**\n\n| Job | Steps |\n| --- | --- |\n| **detect-changes** | Uses `dorny/paths-filter` to detect changes in `cartridges/`, `data/core/`, `data/vendor/`. Resolves target environment. On `workflow_dispatch` uses manually selected flags. |\n| **lint-xml** | Downloads SFCC XSD schemas, runs `node scripts/validate-xml.js` against all XML files in `data/`. Blocks `deploy-data` if any file fails schema validation. |\n| **run-tests** | Runs `npm run lint` and `npm run test`. Must pass before code is deployed. |\n| **deploy-code** | Installs vendor cartridges, zips all cartridges into a timestamped code version (`zimmermann_YYYYMMDD_HHmmss`), uploads via WebDAV, activates on the target instance. Uploads the zip as a GitHub artifact. |\n| **deploy-data** | Zips `data/core/`, uploads and imports to the target instance via `sfcc-ci instance:import`. On success, runs `sfcc-ci job:run RebuildALLSearchIndex` synchronously to rebuild product search across all 8 sites. |\n| **deploy-vendor-data** | Zips and imports `data/vendor/` (Global-e and Avalara metadata). Runs after `deploy-data`. |\n\n**Required GitHub secrets and variables:**\n\n| Name | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client ID |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client secret |\n| `SFCC_INSTANCE` | Variable (env-scoped) | Sandbox hostname, e.g. `bkzk-002.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com` |\n\n---\n\n### cd-test.yml — Scheduled Test Refresh (BKZK-005)\n\n**Triggers:** - **Scheduled:** Runs automatically twice daily — **7:00 am AEST** (21:00 UTC) and **7:00 pm AEST** (09:00 UTC). - **Manual:** `workflow_dispatch` — can be triggered on demand from the GitHub Actions UI at any time.\n\n**Purpose:** Keeps the TEST environment (BKZK-005) continuously up to date with the latest code from `develop` and a clean data import, so QA always has a fresh environment. Every scheduled run performs a full refresh — code deploy, core data import, vendor data import, and search index rebuild.\n\n**Dispatch inputs (manual runs):**\n\n| Input | Description | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `deploy_data` | Import core data | true |\n| `deploy_vendor_data` | Import vendor data (Avalara, Global-e) | true |\n\n**Jobs and execution order:**\n\nnonelint-xml\ntest\n└── deploy-code (needs test)\n└── deploy-data (needs deploy-code + lint-xml)\n├── Rebuild search index\n└── deploy-vendor-data (needs deploy-data)\n\n**Job details:**\n\n| Job | Steps |\n| --- | --- |\n| **lint-xml** | Validates all XML files in `data/` against SFCC schemas. Blocks data import if any file fails. |\n| **test** | Runs `npm run test:coverage`. Must pass before code is deployed. |\n| **deploy-code** | Installs vendor cartridges, zips into a timestamped code version, deploys and activates on BKZK-005. |\n| **deploy-data** | Always runs on schedule. Imports `data/core/` and rebuilds the search index across all 8 sites. |\n| **deploy-vendor-data** | Always runs on schedule. Imports `data/vendor/` (Global-e and Avalara metadata) after core data. |\n\n**Required GitHub environment:** A GitHub environment named `test` with the following scoped secrets and variables:\n\n| Name | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client ID |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client secret |\n| `SFCC_INSTANCE` | Variable | TEST instance hostname, e.g. `bkzk-005.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com` |\n| `SFCC_CODE_VERSION_PREFIX` | Variable | Code version prefix, e.g. `zimmermann` |\n\n---\n\n### cd-release.yml — Release to UAT / Staging\n\n**Triggers:****Manual `workflow_dispatch` only.** Staging and UAT deployments are always controlled — there is no automatic push trigger. Deployments must be initiated deliberately from the GitHub Actions UI or CLI.\n\n**Dispatch inputs:**\n\n| Input | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ref` | Tag or branch to deploy, e.g. `release-1.2.3`, `release/1.2.3`, or `release/release-1.2.3` |\n| `target_environment` | `staging-and-uat` (default), `staging-only`, or `uat-only` |\n| `deploy_data` | Import core data (boolean, default false) |\n| `deploy_vendor_data` | Import vendor data (boolean, default false) |\n\n**Jobs and execution order:**\n\nnonedetect-changes + resolve-version\n├── lint-xml\n├── run-tests\n├── deploy-code-uat → deploy-code-staging\n├── deploy-data-uat → deploy-data-staging\n│ └── Rebuild search index (both UAT and Staging)\n└── deploy-vendor-data-uat → deploy-vendor-data-staging\n\n**Key differences from cd-deploy.yml:** - Extracts a release version from the provided ref (`release/1.2.3` → code version `zimmermann_release_1.2.3`). - Deploys sequentially to UAT first, then Staging — Staging is blocked until UAT succeeds. - Uses environment-scoped GitHub variables (`SFCC_INSTANCE`) to target the correct instance per stage. - Search index rebuild runs after each data import on both UAT and Staging.\n\n### Staging authentication\n\nStaging uses **certificate-based authentication** for code upload (WebDAV) and OAuth client credentials for data import (OCAPI).\n\n| Operation | Auth method | Hostname |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `code:deploy` (WebDAV) | p12 client certificate (`-c`/`-p` flags) | `cert.<SFCC_INSTANCE>` — sfcc-ci automatically adjusts to plain hostname for activation |\n| `instance:upload` (WebDAV data) | OAuth client credentials | `<SFCC_INSTANCE>` |\n| `instance:import` (OCAPI job) | OAuth client credentials | `<SFCC_INSTANCE>` |\n\n**Required secrets for the `staging` GitHub environment:**\n\n| Name | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` | Secret | OAuth client ID for OCAPI (data import) |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` | Secret | OAuth client secret for OCAPI (data import) |\n| `SFCC_CODE_CERT_P12` | Secret | Base64-encoded `.p12` certificate for WebDAV code upload. Generate with: `base64 -i your-cert.p12 \\| pbcopy` |\n| `SFCC_CODE_CERT_PASSPHRASE` | Secret | Passphrase for the `.p12` certificate |\n| `SFCC_INSTANCE` | Variable | Staging hostname, e.g. `staging.yourorg.demandware.net` |\n\n---\n\n### Search index rebuild\n\nAfter every successful core data import (in `cd-deploy.yml`, `cd-test.yml`, and `cd-release.yml`), the workflow runs:\n\nbashnpx sfcc-ci job:run RebuildALLSearchIndex -i $SFCC\\_INSTANCE -s -f\n\n* **Job:**`RebuildALLSearchIndex` (defined in `data/core/jobs.xml`)\n* **Scope:**`<all-storefront-sites/>` — rebuilds product and active data search indexes for all 8 Zimmermann sites in parallel\n* **Flags:**`-s` (synchronous — waits for completion), `-f` (fail-fast — marks the workflow step as failed if the job errors)\n* **Local equivalent:**`npm run search:reindex` (also runs automatically after `npm run data:import:core` and `npm run data:import:sample`)\n\n---\n\nCI/CD tooling reference\n-----------------------\n\n| Tool / resource | Purpose | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GitHub Actions | CI/CD orchestration | Workflows in `.github/workflows/` |\n| SFCC WebDAV API | Cartridge ZIP upload | Certificate-based for staging; OAuth for dev/SIT/UAT/test |\n| OCAPI Data API | Code version management, job execution | Client credentials OAuth: `SFCC_CLIENT_ID`, `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` |\n| sfcc-ci (npm) | CLI wrapper for OCAPI operations | Included as a dev dependency |\n| Jest | Unit testing cartridge scripts | Mocks for `dw.*` APIs; 90% coverage threshold enforced |\n| BM (Business Manager) | Code version UI, import/export, jobs | Admin access required for production |\n| Control Center | Start/stop/create developer sandboxes | CC Admin access required |",
